sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant Ctrl as {Entity}Controller
    participant VB as ValidationBehavior
    participant GB as GuidResolvingBehavior
    participant CB as ConcurrencyBehavior
    participant UWB as UnitOfWorkBehavior
    participant H as Create{Entity}Handler
    participant R as Create{Entity}GuidResolver
    participant DB as Database

    Note over C: Client generates Guid<br/>(e.g. frontend NgRx optimistic store)

    rect rgb(230, 245, 255)
    Note over C,DB: Flow 1 — new Guid, first request
    C->>Ctrl: POST /{entity} { guid, title, assigneeId }
    activate Ctrl
    Ctrl->>VB: Send(Create{Entity}Command)
    activate VB
    VB->>GB: validate input
    activate GB
    GB->>R: ResolveAsync(guid)
    activate R
    R->>DB: SELECT ... WHERE Guid = guid
    activate DB
    DB-->>R: null (not found)
    deactivate DB
    R-->>GB: null
    deactivate R
    GB->>CB: next()
    activate CB
    Note right of CB: create commands do not<br/>implement IHasVersions — skips
    CB->>UWB: next()
    activate UWB
    UWB->>H: depth++
    activate H
    H->>H: create entity, store Guid
    H-->>UWB: Result.Created(Create{Entity}Result)
    deactivate H
    UWB->>DB: SaveChangesAsync(depth == 1)
    activate DB
    DB-->>UWB: success
    deactivate DB
    UWB-->>Ctrl: Result.Created(Create{Entity}Result)
    deactivate UWB
    deactivate CB
    deactivate GB
    deactivate VB
    Ctrl-->>C: 201 Created { id: 42 }
    deactivate Ctrl
    Note over C: Client stores internal Id
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 230)
    Note over C,DB: Flow 2 — duplicate Guid, retry after transient failure
    C->>Ctrl: POST /{entity} { guid, title, assigneeId }
    activate Ctrl
    Ctrl->>VB: Send(Create{Entity}Command)
    activate VB
    VB->>GB: validate input
    activate GB
    GB->>R: ResolveAsync(guid)
    activate R
    R->>DB: SELECT ... WHERE Guid = guid
    activate DB
    DB-->>R: existing entity
    deactivate DB
    R-->>GB: ConflictResult<Create{Entity}Result>
    deactivate R
    GB-->>Ctrl: ConflictResult<Create{Entity}Result>
    deactivate GB
    deactivate VB
    Ctrl->>Ctrl: map ConflictResult<T> to 409
    Ctrl-->>C: 409 Conflict { id: 42 }
    deactivate Ctrl
    Note over C: Client calls GET /{entity}/42 if full data is needed
    end

    rect rgb(255, 230, 230)
    Note over C,DB: Flow 3 — concurrent requests bypass pipeline check
    C->>Ctrl: POST /{entity} { guid, ... }
    activate Ctrl
    C->>Ctrl: POST /{entity} { guid, ... }
    Ctrl->>GB: both reach GuidResolvingBehavior
    activate GB
    GB->>R: ResolveAsync(guid) — both
    activate R
    R->>DB: both return null (race condition)
    activate DB
    DB-->>R: null
    deactivate DB
    R-->>GB: null
    deactivate R
    GB->>UWB: both proceed to handler
    activate UWB
    UWB->>H: both create entity, store Guid
    activate H
    H->>H: process
    H-->>UWB: both return Result.Created
    deactivate H
    UWB->>DB: SaveChangesAsync (first)
    activate DB
    DB-->>UWB: success
    deactivate DB
    UWB->>DB: SaveChangesAsync (second)
    activate DB
    DB--xUWB: PostgresException 23505<br/>unique index UX_{Entity}_Guid
    deactivate DB
    UWB--xCtrl: exception
    deactivate UWB
    deactivate GB
    Ctrl--xC: 500 (or mapped 409 via global exception handler)
    deactivate Ctrl
    Note over DB: DB unique index is the last line of defence
    end
